<context>
Epic EP-001 — Calendar clones through Calendar.app.
Goal: every calendar the Operator owns shows the busy slots of the other calendars, so colleagues on any account
see the real availability and the Operator gets notified on every client.
Architecture: a single Swift executable (`calsyn-cli`, Swift Package `calsyn`) talks to the calendar store
through EventKit and never touches credentials. `runner` serialises reconciles triggered by startup, store
changes and a 5 min timer; `launch-agent` keeps the process alive in the user session through launchd.

Scope of this workflow:
- TASK-007: `calsyn run` stays alive and reconciles at startup, after every calendar store change and every
  5 minutes, one reconcile at a time, reloading the config each time. Components: cli, runner, config-loader.
- TASK-008: `calsyn install` makes launchd keep `calsyn run` alive in the user session; `calsyn uninstall`
  removes it. Components: cli, launch-agent.
- TASK-010: `calsyn config` opens the config file in the macOS default text editor (`open -t`).
  Components: cli.
</context>
<input type="task">alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-007.md</input>
<input type="task">alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-008.md</input>
<input type="task">alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-010.md</input>
<coding_test>
- `swift test`: runner reloads config at every reconcile (AS-15); run on every change.
- Manual E2E: `calsyn run`, edit an event in Calendar.app, check stdout (AS-14); before closing TASK-007.
- Manual E2E: `calsyn install`, `launchctl list`, `tail ~/Library/Logs/calsyn.log`, `calsyn uninstall` (AS-16); before closing TASK-008.
- Manual E2E: `calsyn config` with and without an existing config, and with `--config &lt;path&gt;`; before closing TASK-010.
</coding_test>
<available_agents>
    <agent subagent_type="alligator-llm:developer" id="developer">Implements the code of the tasks and applies the fixes requested by the reviewer.</agent>
    <agent subagent_type="alligator-llm:devils-advocate" id="devils-advocate">Reviews the implementation against the tasks' Definition of Done and the epic's architecture, and reports the gaps to the developer.</agent>
</available_agents>
<tasks>
    <task id="task-007">
        `developer` implements TASK-007. Definition of Done:
        - `calsyn run` logs a reconcile at startup
        - After the Operator edits an event in Calendar.app, the log shows a new reconcile without any command
        - With no changes, the log shows a reconcile every 5 minutes
        - Reconciles never overlap: the log never shows a reconcile starting before the previous one ended
        - After the Operator edits `config.yaml` while `calsyn run` is running, the next reconcile uses the new config without a restart
        `devils-advocate` reviews the result; `developer` applies the fixes until the review passes.
    </task>
    <task id="task-008">
        `developer` implements TASK-008. Definition of Done:
        - `calsyn install` copies the binary to `~/.calsyn/bin`, writes `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.totomz.calsyn.plist` and loads it
        - After `calsyn install`, `launchctl list` shows `com.totomz.calsyn` and `~/Library/Logs/calsyn.log` grows with reconcile lines
        - After a logout/login the agent is running again
        - `calsyn uninstall` unloads the agent and removes the plist: `launchctl list` no longer shows `com.totomz.calsyn`
        `devils-advocate` reviews the result; `developer` applies the fixes until the review passes.
    </task>
    <task id="task-010">
        `developer` implements TASK-010. Definition of Done:
        - `calsyn config` opens `~/.config/calsyn/config.yaml` with `open -t` and exits with code 0
        - `calsyn config --config &lt;path&gt;` opens the given file instead
        - If the file does not exist, `calsyn config` creates it empty (with its parent folders) and opens it
        - If `open -t` fails, calsyn logs an ERROR line naming the path and exits with a code ≠ 0
        `devils-advocate` reviews the result; `developer` applies the fixes until the review passes.
    </task>
    <task id="close-specs">
        Rename `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-007.md` to `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-007-done.md`,
        `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-008.md` to `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-008-done.md` and
        `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-010.md` to `alligator/specs/EP-001/TASK-010-done.md`.
        Update every reference to the old names under `alligator/specs/`.
    </task>
</tasks>
